---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About｜PubMed Trivia"
  description="PubMed Trivia publishes daily trivia and deep-dive articles based on peer-reviewed PubMed papers in psychology and biology. Transparent editorial responsibility and workflow disclosure."
  lang="en"
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <h1>About PubMed Trivia</h1>

    <h2>Site Overview</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>PubMed Trivia</strong> publishes general-reader-friendly articles adapted from
      <strong>peer-reviewed papers</strong> (especially systematic reviews and meta-analyses) in the US National Library of Medicine's
      <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">PubMed</a> database, focused on psychology and biology.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site launched in May 2026 and, as of October 2026, hosts <strong>over 700 articles</strong> in Japanese and English.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial Principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fact-first</strong>: Articles adapt only what the original abstract says. No speculation, no medical advice.</li>
      <li><strong>Primary-source routing</strong>: Every article includes the PMID and source URL so readers can verify the original paper at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Correlation ≠ causation</strong>: Prompts constrain the adaptation model from upgrading "association" to "causation."</li>
      <li><strong>Continuous quality improvement</strong>: Published articles continue to receive editorial-quality improvements. See <a href="/en/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy → Update Log</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Topics Covered</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Psychology, sleep, memory, learning, behavioral economics</li>
      <li>Animal behavior, evolutionary biology, ecology, anthropology, microbiology</li>
      <li>Diet, exercise, and lifestyle associations with health (but not medical advice)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Editorial Responsibility & Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Site name</strong>: PubMed Trivia</li>
      <li><strong>Operation & Editorial Responsibility</strong>: PubMed Trivia Editorial Team</li>
      <li><strong>Editorial Policy</strong>: <a href="/en/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a></li>
      <li><strong>Editor Details</strong>: <a href="/en/editor/">About the Editorial Team</a></li>
      <li><strong>Contact</strong>: <a href="mailto:sciencepubmedjp@gmail.com">sciencepubmedjp@gmail.com</a>
        (we respond to error reports within 48 hours, excluding weekends/holidays)</li>
      <li><strong>Social</strong>:
        <a href="https://x.com/science_pubmed" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">X</a> /
        <a href="https://www.threads.com/@science_pubmed" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">Threads</a> /
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/science_pubmed/" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">Instagram</a> /
        <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/sciencepubmed.bsky.social" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">Bluesky</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      Information on this site is <strong>general-interest science trivia</strong> and
      <strong>not intended as medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment</strong>.
      Please consult qualified healthcare professionals for health-related decisions.
    </p>
    <p>
      We take care in interpreting papers but promptly correct any errors reported.
      See the <a href="/en/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> for the correction workflow.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising & Affiliates</h2>
    <p>
      This site participates in the Amazon Associates program, Moshimo Affiliate, and Google AdSense.
      See the <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
    </p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .about-page { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 20px 60px; }
    .about-page h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 16px; }
    .about-page h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--navy); margin: 28px 0 10px; padding-left: 12px; border-left: 5px solid var(--navy); }
    .about-page p { line-height: 1.9; color: #2d3748; margin: 0 0 14px; }
    .about-page ul { line-height: 1.9; color: #2d3748; padding-left: 24px; }
    .about-page a { color: var(--link); font-weight: 500; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
